Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">, where </span></span><span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"a\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><var mathquill-command-id=\\"21\\">a</var></span></span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\"> is a constant, has exactly one real solution.</span></span><br><span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">What is the value of </span></span><span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"a\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><var mathquill-command-id=\\"21\\">a</var></span></span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[],"correct":"0","solution":""},{"type":"choice","article":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">For data set A, the table summarizes the distribution of the number of pieces of mail received by a business each day during a period of 11&nbsp;days.<br><img src=\\"/images/3a2ac9f1be78964d9cd4a2ad7ffb175f.png\\" style=\\"width: 500px; height: 472px;\\"><br>The data value 14 is removed from data set A to create data set B, which consists of the remaining&nbsp;10 data values. Which statement best compares the median of data set A and the median of data&nbsp;set B?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[{"name":"A","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The median of data set B is greater than the median of data set A.</span></span><br>"},{"name":"B","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The median of data set B is equal to the median of data set A.</span></span><br>"},{"name":"C","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The median of data set B is less than the median of data set A.</span></span><br>"},{"name":"D","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">There is not enough information to compare the medians of the two data sets.</span></span><br>"}],"correct":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The median of data set B is equal to the median of data set A.</span></span><br>","solution":""},{"type":"write","article":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">6<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">x</span></i><i><sup><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\"><span style=\\"vertical-align:super\\">2 </span></span></sup></i>+11=<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">nx</span></i></span></span><br><p style=\\"text-align:justify\\"><span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">In the given equation, <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">n</span></i>&nbsp;is a constant. The equation has exactly one solution. What is the value of&nbsp;<span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"\\\\frac{n^2}{8}\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><span class=\\"mq-fraction mq-non-leaf\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"3\\"><span class=\\"mq-numerator\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"4\\"><var mathquill-command-id=\\"14\\">n</var><span class=\\"mq-supsub mq-non-leaf mq-sup-only\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"10\\"><span class=\\"mq-sup\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"11\\"><span mathquill-command-id=\\"13\\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\\"mq-denominator\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"5\\"><span mathquill-command-id=\\"7\\">8</span></span><span style=\\"display:inline-block;width:0\\">​</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;</span></span><br></p>","question":"","options":[],"correct":"33","solution":""},{"type":"choice","article":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The table gives the areas and perimeters of two similar rectangles, where <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">n</span></i>&nbsp;is a constant.<br><img src=\\"/images/e538564622b1510b6c69b700652cdfe6.png\\" style=\\"width: 500px; height: 87px;\\"><br>What is the value of <em>n</em>?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[{"name":"A","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">740</span></span><br>"},{"name":"B","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">1,480</span></span><br>"},{"name":"C","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">2,960</span></span><br>"},{"name":"D","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">3,700</span></span><br>"}],"correct":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">740</span></span><br>","solution":""},{"type":"write","article":"<img src=\\"/images/f7f70ec824b7fe64057ea5148562b902.png\\" style=\\"width: 500px; height: 303px;\\"><br><span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">In the figure, <span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"\\\\overline{AD}\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><span class=\\"mq-non-leaf mq-overline\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"4\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"3\\"><var mathquill-command-id=\\"6\\">A</var><var mathquill-command-id=\\"7\\">D</var></span></span></span>&nbsp; and <span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"\\\\overline{BC}\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><span class=\\"mq-non-leaf mq-overline\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"4\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"3\\"><var mathquill-command-id=\\"8\\">B</var><var mathquill-command-id=\\"9\\">C</var></span></span></span>&nbsp; intersect at point <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">D</span></i>. The measure of ∠ABD is <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">w</span></i>°, the measure of&nbsp;∠C&nbsp;is <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">z</span></i>°, and <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">AD</span></i>&nbsp;= 143. If cos <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">w</span></i>°= <span class=\\"mq-math-mode\\" latex-data=\\"\\\\frac{9}{41}\\"><span class=\\"mq-textarea\\"><textarea autocapitalize=\\"off\\" autocomplete=\\"off\\" autocorrect=\\"off\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\" data-cke-editable=\\"1\\" spellcheck=\\"false\\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\\"true\\"></textarea></span><span class=\\"mq-root-block\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"1\\"><span class=\\"mq-fraction mq-non-leaf\\" mathquill-command-id=\\"18\\"><span class=\\"mq-numerator\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"19\\"><span mathquill-command-id=\\"22\\">9</span></span><span class=\\"mq-denominator\\" mathquill-block-id=\\"20\\"><span mathquill-command-id=\\"23\\">4</span><span mathquill-command-id=\\"24\\">1</span></span><span style=\\"display:inline-block;width:0\\">​</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;, what is the value of tan <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">z</span></i>°?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[],"correct":"40/9,4.444","solution":""},{"type":"choice","article":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">In triangle <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">XYZ</span></i>, the measure of angle <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">X</span></i>&nbsp;is <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">x</span></i>°, the measure of angle <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">Y</span></i>&nbsp;is <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">y</span></i>°, and the&nbsp;measure of angle <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">Z</span></i>&nbsp;is 17°. If&nbsp;<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">x</span></i>&nbsp;&gt;&nbsp;<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">y</span></i><i>&nbsp;</i>&gt; 17, which of the following additional pieces of information&nbsp;is NOT sufficient to determine the values of <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">x</span></i>&nbsp;and <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">y</span></i>?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[{"name":"A","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The value of 17 -&nbsp;<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">x&nbsp;</span></i>- 3<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">y</span></i></span></span><br>"},{"name":"B","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The value of 17&nbsp;+ 3<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">x</span></i>&nbsp;+&nbsp;<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">y</span></i></span></span><br>"},{"name":"C","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The value of 17-3<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">x</span></i>&nbsp;+&nbsp;3<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">y</span></i></span></span><br>"},{"name":"D","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The value of 17 - 3<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">x&nbsp;</span></i>- 3<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">y</span></i></span></span><br>"}],"correct":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">The value of 17 - 3<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">x&nbsp;</span></i>- 3<i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">y</span></i></span></span><br>","solution":""},{"type":"choice","article":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">In 2007, Elijah earned 17% more than in 2006, and in 2008 Elijah earned 3% more than in&nbsp;2007. If Elijah earned <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">y</span></i>&nbsp;times as much in 2006 as in 2008, which of the following is closest to the&nbsp;value of <i><span style=\\"font-style:italic\\">y</span></i>?</span></span><br>","question":"","options":[{"name":"A","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">0.1765</span></span><br>"},{"name":"B","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">0.5100</span></span><br>"},{"name":"C","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">0.8298</span></span><br>"},{"name":"D","content":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">1.2051</span></span><br>"}],"correct":"<span style=\\"font-size:20px;\\"><span style=\\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif;\\">0.8298</span></span><br>","solution":""}]');export{a as default};
